This project maintains a graphify knowledge graph in `graphify-out/` (see AGENTS.md).

Mandatory every turn:

1. Questions about this project: if `graphify-out/graph.json` exists, run
   `graphify query "<question>"` first and answer from the graph. Read files only for
   details the graph lacks.
2. After creating/modifying/deleting ANY project file: update the graph before ending the
   turn — `/graphify . --update` (graph exists) or `/graphify .` (no graph yet).
3. CLI missing: `uv tool install --upgrade graphifyy` (fallback `pip install graphifyy`),
   then run the pipeline.

Minimal implementation ladder (ponytail, MIT): skip what doesn't need to exist; reuse
codebase/stdlib/native/installed deps before new code; one line when possible; else the
minimum that works. Never cut spec-mandated bodies, validation, error handling, or tests
(docs/01-09 are requirements, not YAGNI candidates). Read the code you touch before you
trim. After each milestone, ask "what did we build the docs didn't ask for?" and delete it
or justify it in docs/01 §5.

A turn that edited files without updating the graph is incomplete.
